  "notes": "Huawei figures for the F1A-8H20Q: 56 physical ports maximum, 8x100GE, 20x25GE (+32 via 100GE breakout), 48x10GE (+32 breakout), 2.4 Tbit/s switching, 453 Mpps, 325 W typical, 2x power 1+1, 4 fans 3+1, 43.6 x 442 x 420 mm (1U). The port map: ports 0-27 are 10GE/GE SFP+ and 10GE WAN capable; 28-35 are 25GE/10GE/GE in two port groups (28-31, 32-35) whose mode changes together; 36-47 are 25GE/10GE only; 48-55 are 100GE/50GE/40GE and are the only ports that break out (port split). Management is separate from the data ports: MGMT-ETH (RJ45), a Console/AUX RJ45 hybrid at 9600 bit/s, TOD and CLK RJ45 clock ports, USB, and two reserved SFP 1G cascade ports (GE0/GE1) - none of those are modelled here. Capacity discrepancy worth stating: the F-series marketing page gives the F1A a maximum capacity of 1.2 Tbit/s (1200 G/U capacity density) while the V800R023C10SPC500 hardware description states 2.4 Tbit/s switching capacity for this chassis; the hardware description is the datasheet of record here. The F-series platform is documented as SR/BNG/CGN/IPSec-capable, which is where nat, firewall and dhcp-server come from. https://support.huawei.com/enterprise/en/doc/EDOC1100382055/ce5c8c83/netengine-8000-f1a-8h20q",
